"""GT-TC048B-H025-L1 - SPST-NO tactile switch, oval actuator, 4.2 x 3.2 x 2.5 mm, SMD-4P.

Datasheet: G-Switch GT-TC048X-HXXX-LX drawing (2019-05-29), LCSC C778165.
Ordering code (drawing, part number key): B = 250 gf operating force,
H025 = 2.5 mm switch height, L1 = 100,000 cycles.

Pins ("CIRCUIT DIAGRAM"): pads 1 and 2 are joined inside the switch, and so are
pads 3 and 4; pressing the actuator closes 1-2 to 3-4. The symbol names pads 1-2
`A` and pads 3-4 `B`, so each side is one net whichever pad the layout routes.

Ratings ("G-Switch Specification"): 50 mA at 24 VDC, contact resistance
100 mohm max, insulation 100 Mohm min at 100 VDC, 250 VAC for 1 min dielectric,
travel 0.20 +/- 0.1 mm, -30 to +85 C.

Footprint: LCSC/EasyEDA land pattern, as in the Altium MicrasLib: pads
1.0 x 0.7 mm at x = +/-2.0 mm, y = +/-1.075 mm (2.15 mm pitch, as drawn). The
datasheet's "P.C.B LAND DIMENSION" puts the 1.0 x 0.7 mm pads at x = +/-2.25 mm
(3.5 mm inner, 5.5 mm outer span); the footprint pads sit 0.25 mm further in,
still under the 4.5 mm lead span. The embedded STEP is a C&K PTS810 model
(same 4.2 x 3.2 mm body, not this part's exact actuator).
"""

A = io(Net)
B = io(Net)

Component(
    name="SW",
    prefix="SW",
    symbol=Symbol(library="GT-TC048B-H025-L1.kicad_sym"),
    footprint=File("SW-SMD-4P_L4.2-W3.2_GT-TC048.kicad_mod"),
    part=Part(mpn="GT-TC048B-H025-L1", manufacturer="G-Switch"),
    pins={
        "A": A,
        "B": B,
    },
)
